      "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[3f(t)-g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =3{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{4}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\,-6,\\,3⟩-⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,4,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-10,\\,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
